Suppose that the joint pdf of $(X, Y)$ is given by

$$
f(x,y)=\begin{cases}
\dfrac{2}{a^2}, & 0\le x\le y\le a\\
\text{elsewhere}
\end{cases}
$$

Find the conditional pdf of $Y=y$ for given $X=x$.

Let $X_1, X_2, \ldots, X_n$ denote a random sample of size $n$ from a distribution having pdf

$$
f(x,\theta)=\begin{cases}
\theta^x(1-\theta)^{1-x}, & 0\le \theta \le 1\\
0, & \text{elsewhere}
\end{cases}
$$

Find the maximum likelihood estimation for $\theta$.
